Backport of upstream PR #402 (github.com/sirrobot01/decypharr), which is open
and unmerged as of v2.5.

TorBox can answer a link-validation request with a bare HTTP 400. The provider
API path in ErrorCodeToLinkError has no case for "400", so it falls through to
the default branch, which classifies the error as PERMANENT. resolveLinkWithRetry
returns immediately on a permanent error, so the 4 attempts and the exponential
backoff are never used, and fetchAndValidate memoises the failure against the
link URL. See docs/TROUBLESHOOTING.md, "TorBox: ... 400: unknown error code: 400".

ClassifyStreamStatus already treats a CDN-layer 400 as refetchable. This makes
the provider-API path agree.

This patch applies to v2.5 and is removed when upstream ships the fix.

diff --git a/pkg/manager/link/errors.go b/pkg/manager/link/errors.go
--- a/pkg/manager/link/errors.go
+++ b/pkg/manager/link/errors.go
@@ -107,6 +107,9 @@ var (
 	Err404 = errors.New("HTTP 404 Not Found")
 	Err429 = errors.New("HTTP 429 Too Many Requests")
 	Err503 = errors.New("HTTP 503 Service Unavailable")
+	// ErrLinkRejected is a 400 from the provider/CDN, which in practice means
+	// the presigned link expired or rotated rather than a malformed request.
+	ErrLinkRejected = errors.New("HTTP 400: link rejected")
 )
 
 // NewLinkError creates a new LinkError with the given error and category
@@ -157,6 +160,14 @@ func ErrorCodeToLinkError(code string) *Error {
 		return NewPermanentError(Err404, code)
 	case "429":
 		return NewRetryableError(Err429, code)
+	// TorBox returns a bare 400 for a presigned link that has expired or
+	// rotated. ClassifyStreamStatus already treats 400 at the CDN layer as
+	// refetchable; the provider-API path must agree, otherwise a stale link is
+	// classified permanent and no retry is ever attempted.
+	case "400":
+		return NewRefetchableError(ErrLinkRejected, code)
 	case "503", "read_pxy_timeout":
 		return NewRetryableError(Err503, code)
 	default:
